    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0404" n="232" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3337</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Mooney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Asuncion</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-15T15:00:00-03:50">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 16, 2.10
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s February 3, 1 p.m. The answer of the Paraguayan Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs states that the unrestricted prosecution of submarine warfare will be
                    greatly damaging to neutral rights, and asks that the attitude of the neutral
                    American states be determined in a convention called to consider the question.
                    Transcript of answer and a translation thereof by mail.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d290-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mooney</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
